{%- comment -%}
  The saving a UGC product card shows (PDP / bundle-page video row and the
  collection grid's UGC tile), as on magyx.whop.site's videos row: against the
  regular (compare-at) price, rounded to a whole percent. No regular price above
  today's = no output = the plain card.

  Outputs "pct|price|compare|per_bottle" (money in cents, per_bottle 0 when the
  title carries no bottle count of 2 or more), or nothing.
  Callers capture it and split on '|':
    {%- capture offer_data -%}{% render 'ugc-offer-data', product: some_product %}{%- endcapture -%}

  Bottle count (German titles): the whole number right before an "x" that is
  followed, with or without a space, by a number and "ml". The pattern may sit
  anywhere in the title and is matched case-insensitively:
    "6 X 50ml Parfümflaschen"            -> 6
    "6X 50ml Parfümflaschen"             -> 6
    "Er & Sie – 2X 50ml Parfümflakons"   -> 2
    "Tagesblüten – 3X 50ml Parfümflakons" -> 3
    "10 X 30ml Parfümflaschen"           -> 10
    "Duftet wie Sauvage - Nr. 366"       -> none
  How: the title is lowercased ("×" counts as "x"), every "x" and every "ml"
  gets a space on each side and runs of spaces are collapsed, so "6X 50ml",
  "6 X 50ml", "6x50ml" and "6 x 50 ml" all become the words "6 x 50 ml". The
  words are then walked: the first "x" whose word before is a whole number, the
  word after a whole number and the next word "ml" gives the count. Splitting
  other words that contain an x or ml ("luxus" -> "lu x us") is harmless, since
  those pieces are never whole numbers. A word is a whole number when adding 0
  and printing it gives the same text back ("06", "2a" and "" are not).

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} the product the card links to
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign offer_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  if offer_variant != blank and offer_variant.compare_at_price > offer_variant.price
    assign offer_pct = offer_variant.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: offer_variant.compare_at_price
    assign offer_pct = 100 | minus: offer_pct | round
    if offer_pct > 0 and offer_pct < 100
      assign bottle_text = product.title | downcase | replace: '×', 'x' | replace: 'x', ' x ' | replace: 'ml', ' ml '
      assign bottle_text = bottle_text | replace: '  ', ' ' | replace: '  ', ' ' | replace: '  ', ' ' | strip
      assign bottle_words = bottle_text | split: ' '
      assign bottles = 0
      for word in bottle_words
        if word != 'x' or forloop.first
          continue
        endif
        assign i_count = forloop.index0 | minus: 1
        assign i_size = forloop.index0 | plus: 1
        assign i_unit = forloop.index0 | plus: 2
        assign w_count = bottle_words[i_count] | append: ''
        assign w_size = bottle_words[i_size] | append: ''
        assign w_unit = bottle_words[i_unit] | append: ''
        assign n_count = w_count | plus: 0
        assign n_size = w_size | plus: 0
        assign s_count = n_count | append: ''
        assign s_size = n_size | append: ''
        if w_unit == 'ml' and s_count == w_count and s_size == w_size and n_count > 0 and n_size > 0
          assign bottles = n_count
          break
        endif
      endfor
      assign offer_per = 0
      if bottles > 1
        assign offer_per = offer_variant.price | times: 1.0 | divided_by: bottles | round
      endif
      echo offer_pct | append: '|' | append: offer_variant.price | append: '|' | append: offer_variant.compare_at_price | append: '|' | append: offer_per
    endif
  endif
-%}
